sau Civil War", "verb": "CAUSES", "targetSlug": "maria-da-conceição-nobre-cabral-diplomatic-role", "targetName": "Maria da Conceição Nobre Cabral's Diplomatic Role", "context": "The aftermath of the 1998-1999 Guinea-Bissau Civil War significantly shaped the context and urgency of Maria da Conceição Nobre Cabral's diplomatic assignments."}, {"sourceSlug": "maria-da-conceição-nobre-cabral", "sourceName": "Maria da Conceição Nobre Cabral", "verb": "INFLUENCES", "targetSlug": "guinea-bissau-us-relations-2000s", "targetName": "Guinea-Bissau-US Relations (2000s)", "context": "As Ambassador to the United States from 2000 to 2006, Maria da Conceição Nobre Cabral directly influenced the bilateral relationship between Guinea-Bissau and the US."}], "places": [{"name": "Bissau, Guinea-Bissau", "role": "Center of political activity"}, {"name": "Washington D.C., United States", "role": "Ambassadorial post"}, {"name": "New York City, United States", "role": "UN Representative post"}], "texts": [{"title": "Wikipedia: Maria da Conceição Nobre Cabral", "type": "Reference article", "slug": "maria-da-conceição-nobre-cabral"}], "externalLinks": ["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q3291098", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maria_da_Concei%C3%A7%C3%A3o_Nobre_Cabral"], "tags": ["Guinea-Bissau", "Political Leaders", "Africa", "political-systems", "geopolitical-linkage", "cause-and-effect"], "thumbnailUrl": "", "quote": "", "legacySummary": "", "historicalSignificance": {"significanceScore": 6, "significanceNarrative": "Maria da Conceição Nobre Cabral played a significant regional role by representing Guinea-Bissau on the international stage during a critical period of post-conflict instability and democratic fragility, contributing to the maintenance of international engagement and aid. Her efforts helped sustain Guinea-Bissau's diplomatic presence amidst profound internal challenges.", "significanceCategory": "regional"}, "_editLog": [{"timestamp": "2026-08-27T11:34:49Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#33067573114", "field": "summary", "oldValue": "Maria da Conceição Nobre Cabral is a Guinea-Bissauan politician who was Minister of Foreign Affairs from 2007 to 2009.", "newValue": "Maria da Conceição Nobre Cabral emerged as a pivotal diplomatic figure for Guinea-Bissau in the early 21st century, serving as the nation's Minister of Foreign Affairs from 2007 to 2009 during a period of profound political volatility. Her career spanned critical ambassadorships to the United States and the United Nations, positioning her at the forefront of Guinea-Bissau's efforts to navigate complex post-conflict reconstruction, regional instability, and the challenges of establishing democratic governance. Her work underscored the persistent fragility of nascent democracies in West Africa and the crucial role of international engagement in their survival.

Prior to her cabinet appointment, Cabral distinguished herself as Guinea-Bissau's Ambassador to the United States and Permanent Representative to the United Nations from 2000 to 2006. In these capacities, she tirelessly advocated for international support, debt relief, and development assistance for her impoverished nation, which had endured a devastating civil war from 1998 to 1999. As Foreign Minister under President João Bernardo Vieira, she was tasked with strengthening bilateral ties, engaging with regional bodies like ECOWAS, and representing Guinea-Bissau's interests amidst a fragile peace, culminating in a period marked by military unrest and a subsequent assassination of the president in March 2009.

